solution_steps:
Let $T$ represent Ted's age and $S$ represent Sally's age.
We can set up a system of equations based on the given information:
\begin{align*}
T &= 2S - 15 \\
T + S &= 54
\end{align*}
We can substitute the first equation into the second equation to solve for $S$:
\begin{align*}
(2S - 15) + S &= 54 \\
3S - 15 &= 54 \\
3S &= 69 \\
S &= 23
\end{align*}
Substituting $S = 23$ into the first equation, we can solve for $T$:
\begin{align*}
T &= 2(23) - 15 \\
T &= 46 - 15 \\
T &= 31
\end{align*}
