input:
Given the function \[f(x) =
\begin{cases}
x/2 &\quad \text{if } x \text{ is even}, \\
3x+1 &\quad \text{if } x \text{ is odd}.
\end{cases}
\]What is the value of $f(f(f(f(1))))$?

solution_steps:
We can simplify the expression using logarithm properties.
\begin{align*}
\log_a \left(\frac{a}{b}\right) + \log_b \left(\frac{b}{a}\right) &= \log_a (a) - \log_a (b) + \log_b (b) - \log_b (a) \\
&= 1 - \log_a (b) + 1 - \log_b (a) \\
&= 2 - \log_a (b) - \log_b (a).
\end{align*}
By the change of base formula, we have
\begin{align*}
\log_a (b) &= \frac{\log_b (b)}{\log_b (a)} = \frac{1}{\log_b (a)}, \\
\log_b (a) &= \frac{\log_a (a)}{\log_a (b)} = \frac{1}{\log_a (b)}.
\end{align*}
Substituting these values back into the expression, we get
\begin{align*}
2 - \log_a (b) - \log_b (a) &= 2 - \frac{1}{\log_a (b)} - \frac{1}{\log_a (b)} \\
&= 2 - \frac{2}{\log_a (b)}.
\end{align*}
Since $a \ge b > 1$, we know that $\log_a (b) < 1$, so $\frac{2}{\log_a (b)} > 2$.
Therefore, the largest possible value of the expression is $\boxed{0}$.
The answer is: 0

